pokeheartgold-speed-spd2.patch (tools/pokehg_gen.py applies the patches in name order): the Transitions setting's HeartGold and
SoulSilver side (docs/speed-options.md "Platinum and HeartGold/SoulSilver"; Platinum's twin is pokeplatinum-speed-spd2.patch).
Each hook asks port/game/speed_gen4.c, which reads `fadespeed` (0 = the game's, 1 = 2x, 2 = 4x, 3 = Instant). At the default
setting each hook is exactly the game's own code path, so the route chain's frames are unchanged.
Fades: unk_0200FA24_0200FA24.c BeginNormalPaletteFade (the one entry of every fade) halves its framesPerStep, then its steps, once
(2x) or twice (4x), or takes one step of one frame (Instant); both stay >= 1 (the asserts' own bound).
The transition window: field_system.c FieldSystem_Main walks the task chain (TaskManager->prev) each field frame and, while a
map-change task is in it, opens libntr's SIM_SetTransition window (the game runs at 2x / 4x, its frames are the same).
field_warp_tasks.c exports PortSpeed4_IsWarpTask, which compares the tasks (its statics: the stairs and warp-panel warps, the
script warp, the special spawn warps, the Union Room's; sub_02055DBC, the door / stairs / escalator / ladder / cave-warp task of
unk_02055BF0.c; PokecenterAnimRun, the healing machine; ov01_021F2944, the Waterfall climb).
Not the new game and continue.
Handover-ID: none (port-only)

